  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-AM6-2 (important, cross-validated by ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa, and arch-qa): the .toml boundary manifests for the dead DaemonRequestDispatcher/ApiRouter/MessageWriter/run_received_hook stack were correctly deleted in commit c07a3a79, but the markdown mirror doc docs/atm-daemon/boundaries.md still describes that dead dispatcher as live. Worse, this same PR's own manifest deletion introduced a NEW dangling link on top of the pre-existing gap -- a regression from this PR's own diff, not merely an unfixed pre-existing issue. arch-qa separately found a second stale section in the same file describing other already-deleted types as still live. The correct fix pattern (retiring a boundary doc section when its manifest is deleted) already exists elsewhere in this same file from earlier AM sprints -- apply that same pattern here." ;
